Subject: =?UTF-8?q?ui/markdown:=20render=20$=E2=80=A6$,=20$$=E2=80=A6$$=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?and=20\[=E2=80=A6\]=20math?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The KaTeX extension only accepted \(…\) inline and $$ on lines of their own,
while models mostly write $…$ inline and $$…$$ on one line, so their math
showed as raw TeX. Accept those forms too, plus \[…\] display math.

Inline $…$ follows Pandoc's rule so prices stay literal: no space just inside
the dollars and no digit right after the closing one ($5 and $10, $5-$6).

Ocelot-Patch: web/math-delimiters

